I haven’t much experience under my belt as a trader. About a year of experience. In school they didn’t teach me about 401Ks, managing your Roth, the different IRAs and such. Here on this app I get to learn and see how people grow and manage their portfolios.

I get to be inspired by the whales and others, and to form friendships with others. However, trading can be daunting. What I do know is how to take a punch or two. https://medium.com/age-of-awareness/what-becoming-paralyzed-taught-me-about-myself-3742ccbbadc7

I experienced a many great loss in my life, both physically and mentally. And have found trading to be a hobby that keeps me grounded. But I treat it as a hobby that keeps pushing me forward.

Like many of you, I rode down some random wave that eventually led me to the Wallstreetbets Reddit, to the Road to 10M Reddit (this app’s sub reddit) and then to this app; and beyond. How ever you yourself ended up on this app: we’re all part of this small microcosms of a community trying to better ourselves financially. 

I learned all about trading through this app and the OA community. Schooling myself and taking notes.

Never before did I know what Greeks were. Or derivatives. Options. Or leverage. This app in itself opened a can of worms for me to sink my teeth into. To educate myself and to better my financial literacy. And with that I’ve grown as a person. I’m more economically in tune with the state of affairs. I understand the markets better and I’m more proactive in my financial being than before.

Now, I’m here with you sharing a bit of my story. 

So, let’s talk about trading and the mental side of things. Something that’s not talked about enough. We teach ourselves how to calculate the Greeks, the standard deviation, moving averages but what we neglect is taking care of one’s mental health. How are you feeling before you press that buy / sell button? 

What are we actually doing? Why do we do this? What is the point of trading? Where is my mental health at? And vice versa. Questions that can save you money adnaseum.  

There’s a plethora of things that we need to consider when trading when we go long or short but there’s one key element that can take you from just being a trader that can execute trades to becoming an exceptional trader.

That’s having mental fortitude to realize you’re FOMOING, revenge trading, and or falling into addictive patterns that can lead you to becoming a gambling addict. So for everyone here on Afterhours please look after yourself. Have some introspection and build your mental muscle just as much as you are with your trading skills to really solidify yourself as a calculated trader and less of a “calculated gambler that got lucky”. 

I turned $200 over the course of a year to near 70k as a slow burn. I didn’t yolo any “plays” to get lucky and I bit the dust by putting skin in the game. But I knew the risks and have had to face the consequences of my actions. Don’t invest without researching. Don’t compare your gains to others. Know at the end of the day. Having a sharp mental outlook paired with investing and or trading options needs to be guided with precision. Take stock of how you’re feeling before you start the day sending your money into the ether.

Slow progress is still progress. Be happy you TP, and or you had good risk management. And if the heat starts to turn up a little too much. Go outside and touch grass. Appreciate what you have, and last but not least. Do not gamble away your rents money! 

Trading and investing can be rewarding and or devastating. And it is that thin razor line that you have to balance to ensure you don’t destroy your mental well being and financially security 🫡

You are not the exit liquidity. 

We’re here to make money, but we mustn’t lose ourselves along the way. It’s okay: another day, another dollar as ABJ would say. 

These people below have shaped me into a better trader and because of this app I’ve made friendships across the internet because @sirjack has turned trading into a less solo activity and made it a mission to allow anyone to come learn, and connect with like minded individuals.

So, look out for one another. We’re all in this together. 🤝

