Whether you bled a lot, or roided up in gains today! We live to fight another day! Trading isn’t an easy sport, and the markets behave erratically due to unforeseen catalysts: geopolitical, climate, socioeconomic, macroeconomic, advancements in tech (DeepSeek) and more.

If you’re actively trading and manage your portfolio daily then blips of big losses are nothing to worry about. Time heals all wounds. Your risk management is measured in where you’re holdings mostly are. Are you heavily titled in tech or are you diversified enough to survive big waves of changes. Are you softening the blow by being a $VTI, or $VOO, VanGuard person with a longer time horizon or are you deep in $SPY and $VGT looking at massive percentile drops.

At the end of the day we’re all on our journey to better ourselves financially. To treat trading as a sport, and or to make it something that unlocks the potential for financial flexibility and freedom. Whomever,  trader you are: just know days like today suck but are also advantageous in being able to scoop things up for the cheap!

